{"id": "EUVD-2026-103468", "enisaUuid": "d17e0e50-236c-315d-80f7-c037860da658", "description": "Omnigent 0.3.0 before 0.14.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows authenticated users to escape the workspace by setting os_env.cwd on nested sub-agents. Attackers can upload a bundle whose sub-agent uses an absolute or parent-traversing working directory, bypassing root-only validation in bundles.py, to read and write host files as the runner user.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:23:31", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/security/advisories/GHSA-p5x3-3gqh-x44g", "https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/blob/v0.13.0/omnigent/server/bundles.py#L138-L155", "https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/commit/4a406d5b3b3f3a7c3401eab659ab04e728923b94", "https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/releases/tag/v0.14.0", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/omnigent-0.3.0-before-0.14.0-path-traversal-via-sub-agent-os-env-cwd"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vg9j-3mjv-5cq3", "CVE-2026-112015"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a4e4fd0e-f91f-35e3-a8fd-36786c772d14", "product": {"name": "omnigent", "vendor": {"name": "omnigent-ai"}}, "product_version": "0.3.0 <0.14.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "15ffa28d-3978-346b-ac60-6aadc6b98c9e", "vendor": {"name": "omnigent-ai"}}], "isExploited": false}